    {
      "id": "akq2vz8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.5 High Court of Madhya Pradesh"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yhimwmq",
      "content": "The High Court of Madhya Pradesh is located at Jabalpur. It was established in 1956. The High Court has benches at Gwalior and Indore. The Chief Justice of the High Court is appointed by the President of India in consultation with the Chief Justice of India and the Governor of Madhya Pradesh. The High Court exercises original, appellate, and supervisory jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "id": "ccznu6a",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.6 District Administration"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bcenrpr",
      "content": "Madhya Pradesh is divided into 10 Divisions and 55 Districts (as of 2023). Each district is headed by a District Magistrate (DM) / Collector who is an IAS officer. The Collector is responsible for law and order, revenue collection, and overall administration of the district."
    },
