    {
      "id": "2mklxxk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3.8 Urban Local Bodies"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rhkh84x",
      "content": "Urban local self-government in Madhya Pradesh is governed by the 74th Constitutional Amendment and the Madhya Pradesh Municipal Corporation Act and Municipalities Act. Urban areas are classified into Nagar Panchayats, Nagar Palika Parishads, and Municipal Corporations (Nagar Nigam) based on their population size. MP has several major Municipal Corporations including Bhopal, Indore, Jabalpur, Gwalior, Ujjain, Rewa, Satna, and others."
    }
